UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): FASB Concepts Statement No. 6 defines ten elements of financial statements for business enterprises: assets, liabilities, equity, revenues, expenses, gains, losses, investments by owners, distributions to owners, and comprehensive income. These elements form the building blocks for recognition and measurement under the FASB conceptual framework.
Wrong (A): Five understates the count by omitting elements such as gains, losses, investments by owners, distributions to owners, and comprehensive income.
Wrong (B): Seven is not the number defined; the statement identifies exactly ten distinct elements.
