-- Q12278: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 505-10-S99 and general FASB guidance, an accumulated deficit is a negative retained earnings balance indicating that cumulative net losses and dividends declared have exceeded cumulative net income since the entity''s inception. It appears as a deduction in stockholders'' equity.
Wrong (A): An accumulated deficit reflects cumulative earnings performance, not the company''s cash position. A firm can have positive cash balances while carrying an accumulated deficit.
Wrong (C): A decline in total asset fair value is an impairment or valuation issue, not the definition of an accumulated deficit.
Wrong (D): Goodwill impairment is a specific write-down of a single intangible asset and is unrelated to the retained earnings balance.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12278;

-- Q12280: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 280-10-50-12, an operating segment is separately reportable if it meets any one of three 10% quantitative thresholds: revenue, reported profit or loss, or assets. Alpha meets the revenue test at 10.5% and Beta meets the profit test at 15.4%, so both are reportable.
Wrong (B): Beta does meet the profit threshold at 15.4%, so it cannot be excluded. Meeting one test is sufficient.
Wrong (C): A segment needs only one threshold, not multiple. Alpha''s revenue alone qualifies it, and the claim that revenue is insufficient alone is incorrect.
Wrong (D): The standard requires only one of the three tests to be met, not all three simultaneously.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12280;

-- Q12281: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 740-20-45, intraperiod tax allocation apportions the total income tax provision for a period among components of comprehensive income, including continuing operations, discontinued operations, other comprehensive income, and items charged to equity. Each component reflects its own tax effect.
Wrong (B): Allocating tax among jurisdictions is interperiod or jurisdictional allocation, not intraperiod tax allocation.
Wrong (C): Spreading tax evenly across interim periods describes the estimated annual effective tax rate method under ASC 270, a separate concept.
Wrong (D): Matching deferred tax assets and liabilities with temporary differences relates to interperiod allocation under ASC 740-10, not intraperiod allocation.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12281;

-- Q12284: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 450-30-25-1, when a loss and a virtually certain insurance recovery relate to the same event, the recovery is recognized up to the loss amount. Hartfield reports the net $50,000 loss ($400,000 minus $350,000) in the period of the casualty.
Wrong (B): Presenting the gross loss and recovery as separate line items for a single casualty event would overstate both gains and losses and is not required under GAAP.
Wrong (C): Deferring the recovery is inappropriate when the insurance confirmation makes it virtually certain in the current period.
Wrong (D): Extraordinary item classification was eliminated by ASU 2015-01, so this presentation is no longer permitted under U.S. GAAP.$EXPL$
