-- Q12287: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under the FASB conceptual framework (SFAC 5 and ASC 220), the income statement reports financial performance over a period by presenting revenues, expenses, gains, and losses to arrive at net income. It is the statement specifically designed to measure periodic performance.
Wrong (B): The balance sheet reports financial position at a point in time, showing assets, liabilities, and equity rather than periodic performance.
Wrong (C): The statement of cash flows reports cash inflows and outflows, not accrual-basis revenues, expenses, gains, and losses.
Wrong (D): The statement of stockholders'' equity shows changes in equity accounts, including retained earnings and contributed capital, not the detail of revenues and expenses.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12287;

