-- Q12292: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 330-10, cost of goods sold for a manufacturer includes all inventoriable product costs: direct materials, direct labor, and manufacturing overhead. These costs attach to inventory and flow to COGS when goods are sold.
Wrong (B): Selling and marketing expenses are period costs expensed as incurred under ASC 720 and are not inventoriable product costs.
Wrong (C): Interest expense on a plant mortgage is a period cost, not a product cost. Only in limited cases under ASC 835-20 can interest be capitalized during construction, not during ongoing operations.
Wrong (D): Research and development costs are expensed as incurred under ASC 730 and are never included in inventory or COGS.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12292;

-- Q12293: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 505-10-50-3, cumulative preferred dividends in arrears must be disclosed in the notes or on the face of the balance sheet, but a liability is not recognized until the board formally declares the dividend. Undeclared dividends do not create a legally enforceable obligation.
Wrong (A): Cumulative preference does not create an automatic liability. A board declaration is required before a dividend payable can be recorded.
Wrong (C): Mandatory redemption affects the classification of the preferred stock itself, not whether undeclared dividends are accrued as a liability.
Wrong (D): Dividends in arrears do not reduce retained earnings. Retained earnings is only reduced when dividends are declared, not merely accumulated.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12293;

