-- Q12300: Statement of Cash Flows [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 230-10-45-28, equity-method income exceeding dividends received is noncash. Net income includes $240,000 of equity income, but only $90,000 was received in cash. The $150,000 excess must be subtracted from net income to reconcile to operating cash flows.
Wrong (A): Adding $240,000 and subtracting $90,000 as gross adjustments overstates the reconciling items. The standard approach nets to a single $150,000 subtraction.
Wrong (C): Adding $90,000 would double-count the cash dividend, which is already reflected in net income through the equity-method pick-up.
Wrong (D): Subtracting the full $240,000 and adding $90,000 reverses the correct direction. The equity income is removed and the dividend added, but this produces the same net $150,000 subtraction as choice B, yet misstates the mechanics.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12300;

-- Q12301: Statement of Cash Flows [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 842 and ASC 230-10-45-28, both the operating lease ROU amortization and the finance lease ROU depreciation are noncash charges that reduced net income without consuming cash. Both amounts are added back to net income under the indirect method, similar to depreciation of tangible assets.
Wrong (B): Operating lease ROU amortization is also a noncash charge and must be added back. Excluding it would understate operating cash flows.
Wrong (C): Finance lease ROU depreciation is treated identically to PP&E depreciation and requires the same add-back adjustment.
Wrong (D): Lease liability reductions reflect the principal portion of cash payments and are separate from the noncash ROU amortization and depreciation adjustments.$EXPL$
