-- Q12302: Statement of Cash Flows [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 230-10-45-28, goodwill impairment is a noncash charge that reduced net income but did not consume cash. It must be added back to net income in the operating activities section under the indirect method, identical to depreciation and amortization.
Wrong (A): Subtracting the impairment would double-count the charge already deducted in net income, further understating operating cash flows.
Wrong (B): Although goodwill relates to a prior acquisition, the impairment charge is a noncash income statement item requiring adjustment in operating activities.
Wrong (C): Goodwill impairment is not a cash outflow at all, so reporting it as an investing outflow would misstate investing activities.$EXPL$
