  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 230-10-45-12(d), COLI policies are investment assets, so the entire $750,000 death benefit is classified as an investing inflow. Under the indirect method, the $460,000 gain included in net income would be subtracted from operating activities to avoid double-counting.
Wrong (A): Although COLI involves an insurance contract, the policy is an investment asset. The nature of the underlying asset, not the contract type, determines classification.
Wrong (B): Splitting the proceeds between investing and operating based on CSV versus gain is incorrect. ASC 230 classifies the full insurance proceeds as investing.
