-- Q12311: Statement of Cash Flows [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 860 and ASC 230, Scenario A qualifies as a sale, so the receivables are derecognized and the $570,000 replaces the normal collection cycle as an operating inflow. In Scenario B, the transfer is a secured borrowing, so the $570,000 is a financing inflow because the receivables remain on the balance sheet.
Wrong (A): Only Scenario A is operating. Scenario B retains the receivables on the books, making the cash advance a financing activity, not operating.
Wrong (C): Neither scenario involves investing. Receivables factoring classified as a sale produces operating cash, not investing cash.
Wrong (D): Only Scenario B is financing. Treating both as financing ignores the sale treatment that applies when recourse is absent and derecognition criteria are met.$EXPL$
