  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 230, the indirect method adjusts for changes in operating liabilities. The warranty liability increased by $35,000 ($180,000 accrued minus $145,000 paid), and increases in operating liabilities are added to net income because cash outflows were less than the expense recognized.
Wrong (B): Subtracting $35,000 reverses the correct direction. A liability increase means less cash was paid than was expensed, requiring an addition.
