-- Q12317: Statement of Cash Flows [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 230-10-45-25, the direct method reports major classes of gross operating cash receipts and payments. Depreciation involves no cash payment, so it is not reported in the operating section under the direct method.
Wrong (A): Adding depreciation to net income is the indirect method treatment. The direct method does not start with net income.
Wrong (B): Depreciation never represents a cash outflow under either method. Listing it as a separate operating payment would overstate cash disbursements.
